884259, "top": [["*", -0.000786733056884259], ["*(", -8.786476135253906]]}, {"t": "  ", "lp": -0.00012839664123021066, "top": [["  ", -0.00012839664123021066], [" **", -9.966285705566406]]}, {"t": " **", "lp": -0.00013733853120356798, "top": [[" **", -0.00013733853120356798], [" **-", -9.581170082092285]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -5.3884050430497155e-05, "top": [["`", -5.3884050430497155e-05], [" `-", -11.185453414916992]]}, {"t": "-", "lp": -0.0001959396613528952, "top": [["-", -0.0001959396613528952], ["C", -9.511520385742188]]}, {"t": "DC", "lp": -0.0004339563602115959, "top": [["DC", -0.0004339563602115959], ["D", -7.812926292419434]]}, {"t": "MAKE", "lp": -4.875778904533945e-05, "top": [["MAKE", -4.875778904533945e-05], ["Make", -11.620201110839844]]}], "text": "Here is a step-by-step breakdown of the `build()` function in your PKGBUILD.\n\n### 1. Environment Setup\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\nset -e\n```\n*   **`source /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force`**: This script sets up the environment variables required for Intel OneAPI tools (like `icx`, `icpx`, and MKL libraries) to work correctly. The `--force` flag ensures it overrides any existing conflicting variables.\n*   **`set -e`**: This is a standard bash safety measure. It causes the script to exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero exit code (an error). This prevents the build from continuing with broken state if a step fails.\n\n### 2. CMake Configuration\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja \\\n```\n*   **`cmake`**: Invokes the CMake build system generator.\n*   **`-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"`**: Specifies the **source directory**. This is where the downloaded git repository code lives.\n*   **`-B \"${srcdir}/build\"`**: Specifies the **build directory**. CMake will generate all intermediate files (object files, makefiles, etc.) here, keeping the source tree clean.\n*   **`-G Ninja`**: Sets the build backend to **Ninja**. Ninja is generally faster than Make for large C++ projects like llama.cpp.\n\n### 3. Compiler & Build Type Flags\n```bash\n    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \\\n    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib \\\n```\n*   **`-DCMAKE"}